// test-adr: 010
// ADR-010: a quoted C-Next include naming a file that is not there is E0506.
//
// #1322: this rule had NO fixture. It reached the user as
// `1:0 Code generation failed: Error: Included C-Next file not found` -- no
// code to look up, and the wrong line. It is also the only thing that fails
// the build for this mistake: discovery warns about the same file and returns,
// so the run would exit 0 without it.
//
// Three negative controls, each closing a different way to get this wrong:
//   - a system header, which is not quoted and not C-Next;
//   - a C-Next file that DOES exist beside this one, so a rule firing on
//     `.cnx` rather than on absence would flag it;
//   - a quoted HEADER that is missing, which is not this rule's business --
//     discovery warns about it and the build continues. Without this line the
//     extension test below is unobservable: mutating it away reddened nothing,
//     because every other quoted include in the corpus names a file that is
//     actually there.

#include <stdint.h>
#include "cnx-alt-helper.cnx"
#include "no-such-header.h"
#include "no-such-file.cnx"

void test() {}
